    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/7b4d46640230aa16863cc2819604d75e-Screenshot 2025-04-02 at 7.41.41 AM.png",
    "name_suffix": "_launch",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Intent:** Students are building a vocabulary of CSS properties so they can translate visual intuitions (\"I want it to feel warm\") into specific instructions (\"use a dark orange color for the headings\"). \r\n\r\n**Circulation questions:**\r\n\r\n- \"How would you describe what this property does in your own words?\"  \r\n- \"How does knowing this property change how you'd write a prompt for AI?\"\r\n\r\n**Expected mistakes and misconceptions:**\r\n\r\n- Students may apply styles randomly rather than intentionally \\- ask them \"why did you choose that color? What feeling were you going for?\"  ",
